## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical application of phishing-resistant MFA and device-based access in admin contexts, plus rollout, exceptions, and measurable outcomes.

## Key Concepts

- phishing-resistant MFA (FIDO2/WebAuthn)
- passwordless SSO
- device posture (MDM/EMM)
- conditional access rules
- centralized logging (SIEM) and phishing simulations

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example simple authorization gate
function allowAccess(user, device) {
  const okUser = user.isAdmin;
  const okDevice = device.isCompliant;
  const okMFA = user.mfaCompletedWithFido2;
  return okUser && okDevice && okMFA;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle a lost FIDO key or key compromise?
- What metrics would you track to gauge phishing-resistant MFA effectiveness?

## Why This Is Asked
The question probes practical edge device security, supply chain controls, and IR readiness for OTA updates in a fleet setting.

## Key Concepts
- Hardware root of trust and device attestation
- Per-release key rotation and role separation
- SBOMs and artifact signing for OTA safety
- OTA gateway revocation and device rollback
- Incident response, containment, and forensics timelines

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation: verify OTA signature before flash
function verifyAndApply(image, publicKey) {
  const ok = verifySignature(image, publicKey);
  if (!ok) throw new Error('Invalid OTA signature');
  flash(image);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale key rotation across millions of devices?
- What logging and forensics data would you collect for IR?
